WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.130
- [Narrator] Queens, New York
is the most ethnically diverse

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.840
urban area in the world.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.240
With over 150 countries represented

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.450
and 138 different languages spoken,

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.250
a subway fare can transport you

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.670
almost anywhere in the world.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.870
And that means that there

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.110
is a lot of great food to be eaten here.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.523
A lot.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.610
Flushing, Queens, is one
of the largest Chinatowns

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:29.490
in the world.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.970
And here you can find a dish

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.003
that stands out due to
something special: it's color.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.328
Over in Jackson Heights we
head south of the border

00:01:37.328 --> 00:01:40.133
and find a flavorful seafood
dish in a very unlikely place.

00:02:37.604 --> 00:02:39.410
In Corona there's a stand embracing

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.040
the flavors of the South Pacific

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.573
and bringing back an old
street food tradition.

00:03:41.907 --> 00:03:44.070
In a different part of
Corona, near the 7 train,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.867
is a small shop serving
up extremely large tortas.

00:04:44.473 --> 00:04:46.061
Finally, back in Jackson Heights,

00:04:46.061 --> 00:04:47.440
in an area called Little Nepal,

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.370
we feast on a traditional dish

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.343
bursting with flavor and history.

